            <td colspan="9" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">(Note 1) Current Tax Payable Included in Retained Earnings - As a limited liability company, we do not directly pay federal income tax. Our taxable income or loss is included in the federal income tax returns of our parent. However, the FERC establishes the method of accounting for income taxes, which permitted the accrual of income taxes on a pass-through entity. In our balance sheet, our income tax liabilities have been calculated as if we were filing a separate return. Current tax payable is relieved through retained earnings as a settlement with our parent.</span>
